{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.stokes_sector_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.stokes_sector_count","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L252-L260","doc":"**The Stokes space is two-dimensional** at `p ≠ 1`: exactly two roots, hence\nexactly two sectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_distinct_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_distinct_iff","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L227-L250","doc":"**The two sectors are distinct exactly when `p ≠ 1`.** At `p = 1` the blocks\ncollide — the classical, non-`q`-deformed limit, which is also the only place\nthe untwisted convention would have agreed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.leading_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.leading_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L200-L225","doc":"**The leading blocks.** For `p > 0` with `p² ≥ 1`, the solutions of the\ntwisted edge equation are `B₁,₂ = ±√((p²−1)/p³)`. In the unramified variable\n`q = p²` that is `±√(q−1)/q^{3/4}` — **not** `±√(q−1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_prod","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L191-L194","doc":"The two roots **multiply to** `−(p²−1)/p³`, division-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_sum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.blocks_sum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L188-L189","doc":"The two roots of the edge polynomial **sum to zero** — it is even in `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.untwisted_forces_trivial_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.untwisted_forces_trivial_p","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L171-L186","doc":"**The untwisted root is not merely a different convention — it is wrong\nexcept in the classical limit.**\n\nIf some `S ≠ 0` satisfied *both* the untwisted edge equation `p⁴S² = p²−1` and\nthe correct one `p³S² = p²−1`, then `p = 1`. So the two disagree at every\n`p ≠ 1`, and the old answer cannot be recovered by renaming. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.edge_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.edge_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L164-L169","doc":"**The edge equation.** With the theta twist, the `i = 2` coefficient `p⁴`\nbecomes `p⁴·p^{−1} = p³`, so the edge polynomial is `p³T² − p² + 1` and the\nedge equation is `p³T² = p² − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_eq_zero_of_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_eq_zero_of_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L155-L158","doc":"**The twist is trivial below `i = 2`.** This is why the error was invisible\nin the two lower-order terms and bit only at `τ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_three","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_two","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_one","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp_zero","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.twistExp","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L147-L148","doc":"The theta-twist exponent `i(i−1)/2` in `θ_p(pⁱw) = p^{i(i−1)/2} wⁱ θ_p(w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.ramification_index_eq_slope_denominator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.ramification_index_eq_slope_denominator","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The ramification index is exactly the denominator of the original slope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.ramified_slope_is_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.ramified_slope_is_integral","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L130-L133","doc":"**Ramification integralises the slope**: index `2` sends `−1/2` to `−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.unramified_slope_not_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.unramified_slope_not_integral","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L120-L128","doc":"**The unramified slope is not an integer** — the precise statement of the\nobstruction that forces ramification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.unramified_slope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.unramified_slope","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L116-L118","doc":"**The unramified slope is `−1/2`.** Non-integral: this is the obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.middle_strictly_above_chord_ramified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.middle_strictly_above_chord_ramified","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L112-L114","doc":"The same after ramification — the hull is still a single edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.middle_strictly_above_chord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.middle_strictly_above_chord","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L107-L110","doc":"**The middle point is not a vertex.** `2·v₁ > v₀ + v₂`, so `(1, 0)` lies\nstrictly above the chord and the lower hull is the single edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.vInfRamified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.vInfRamified","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L100-L105","doc":"`v_∞` after the index-`2` ramification `x = z²`: only `a₂` moves, its\ndegree in `z` doubling from `1` to `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.vInf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Ramified.vInf","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1RamifiedLeadingBlocks.lean#L93-L98","doc":"`v_∞` of the coefficients of `L₁ = (q²x−1)σ² − (q−1)σ − (q−1)`, indexed by\nthe power of `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}